  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The box – first-time passing 4 v 1 and 4 v 2",
  "description": "Set out a square of four cones, a few metres a side. A, B, C and D stand one in each corner and a defender, X, is inside the square. The corner players pass to each other, to the nearest corner or diagonally across the square, and may only play first time. X tries to intercept or touch the ball.\n\nIf X wins the ball, or it leaves the square, X swaps places with the player who made the pass. Play rounds of a couple of minutes and count passes in a row.\n\nStep two: a second defender goes in and the corner players may now take two touches – receive and pass. When the defenders win the ball, the player who made the bad pass goes in and the defender who has been in longest takes the corner. More players: set up two squares side by side. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Find the open passing lane before the ball reaches you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A firm, flat pass off the blade – a bouncing ball gives the defender time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "When the defender presses on the edge, the diagonal across the square is usually open."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "With two touches: receive so the ball is set for the next pass."
    }
  ],
